      },
      "message": "test(ci): dirty-profile proof must occupy the fleet-state tmp the Browser actually writes\n\nThe check dirtied only metaengine-fleet-state-v1.json.tmp, but fleetStatePath()\nin apps/metaengine-browser/src/main.mjs has resolved to\nmetaengine-fleet-state-v2.json since 90b9082a (2026-09-08). The occupation was\ntherefore a silent no-op: Fleet persistence succeeded, the boot emitted no\nSUBSYSTEM_DEGRADED/FLEET evidence, and this proof failed deterministically with\nshell_first_fleet_degradation_evidence_missing (reproduced twice on this PR\nhead, including a full job re-run; local head boot verified that occupying the\nv2 tmp emits the expected EISDIR degradation line while a v1-only occupation\nleaves FLEET SUBSYSTEM_READY).\n\nOccupy both filename generations and document the requirement to keep the list\nin sync with fleetStatePath().",
